# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vl-directory-files-dot-entries-and-default-selector -- "." and ".." are entries, and the default selector is 0
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-11-04

* Symptom

clautolisp's =vl-directory-files= differs from AutoCAD and BricsCAD in two
ways:

1. It never returns ="."= and =".."=. AutoCAD and BricsCAD do: they are
   directory entries like the others, and the patterns ="*"= and ="*.*"=
   match them (pjb, 2026-11-04). clautolisp lists only real files and
   subdirectories (UIOP:DIRECTORY-FILES / UIOP:SUBDIRECTORIES).
2. With the =directories= selector omitted or nil, it lists FILES ONLY
   (it treats nil as 1). Autodesk documents 0 -- files AND directories --
   as the default, and the three products do so.

* Vendor evidence

Error-processing catalogue (probes/error-processing/, case 464,
=(vl-directory-files nil nil)=, 2026-11-03; raw logs under
probes/error-processing/results/raw/):

| product                    | result (first entries)                                             |
|----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------|
| AutoCAD 2022 accoreconsole | ("." ".." "03-11-2026_...dmp" "acc22-lancement-1" ... ) files+dirs |
| BricsCAD V25 Windows       | ("." ".." "acc22-lancement-1" ... "drive-win.sh" ...) dirs, then files |
| BricsCAD V26 macOS         | ("." ".." "lancement-1" "repro-reverse" ... "bc-stdout.txt" ...)  |
| clautolisp 2.3.81          | ("bad.dcl" "bc-stdout.txt" ...) files only, no dot entries         |

=probes/sources/probe-commands.lsp= (cad-probe--find-addon) already relies
on the vendors returning ".." under the -1 selector: it skips it explicitly.

The order of the other entries differs between the products (AutoCAD: name
order; BricsCAD V25: directories first; V26: directory order) and is not
specified; ="."= and =".."= come first on all three.

* Classification

Case 0, *Common*: the three products agree and the Autodesk reference
gives 0 as the default. No warning in any dialect.

* To do

1. Default selector: nil / omitted = 0 (files and directories).
2. ="."= and =".."= are directory entries, listed first, and filtered by
   the pattern like any other name: ="*"= and ="*.*"= (which clautolisp
   already folds to ="*"=) match them, ="*.lsp"= does not. The selector 1
   (files only) excludes them, -1 and 0 include them.
3. Tests: builtin-vl-directory-and-filename-helpers and
   builtin-vl-directory-selector-ignores-trailing-separator assert the
   vendor answer; a new test for the patterns.
4. Spec: VL-DIRECTORY-FILES entry, the default and the dot entries, with
   the probe evidence. User manual: nothing to add (language surface).
5. RELEASE_NOTES, DEVELOP bump.

* Resolved (clautolisp 2.3.84 / alfe 2.3.84, 2026-11-04)

- DIRECTORY-SELECTOR-KIND: nil / omitted is 0 (files and directories).
- COLLECT-DIRECTORY-ENTRIES: "." and ".." are offered first, through the
  same WILDCARD-MATCH-P as the other names, whenever directories are
  selected; then the files, then the subdirectories.
- Tests (builtin-tests.lisp): BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-FILES-DOT-ENTRIES-FOLLOW-
  PATTERN-AND-SELECTOR (new: nil / 0 / -1 / 1 selectors, "*", "*.*",
  "*.lsp", ".."), and BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-AND-FILENAME-HELPERS /
  BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-SELECTOR-IGNORES-TRAILING-SEPARATOR now expect the
  vendor answer. Red before the fix, green after.
- Spec 0.14.6: VL-DIRECTORY-FILES default, dot entries, Tested Behaviour
  (case 464) and the clautolisp note. RELEASE_NOTES entry.
